## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design low-latency multimodal inference on TF Serving, including shared encoders, caching, and batch policy.

## Key Concepts
- Multimodal architecture; dynamic batching; caching; TF-TRT; canary updates

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo config sketch
model_config_list {
  config {
    name: 'multimodal'
    dynamic_batching {
      max_batch_size: 64
      batch_queue_capacity: 128
      fbatch_timeout_micros: 50000
      num_batch_threads: 4
      allow_precision_loss: true
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure tail latency and instrument per-queue metrics?
- How would you invalidate cached image embeddings when inputs change?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests knowledge of production-grade model serving, stateful components, and zero-downtime updates under streaming data.

## Key Concepts

- Embedding sharding and stateful serving
- Online updates without stale reads
- Atomic model version swaps and canary deployment
- Observability, SLAs, rollback strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: versioned embedding cache lookup
const version = process.env.MODEL_VERSION || 'v1';
const embedCache = loadEmbeddingCache(version);

function predict(inputIds) {
  const emb = embedCache.lookup(inputIds);
  return model.apply(emb);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test zero-downtime swap guarantees?
- What race conditions could arise and how would you mitigate them?
